  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Beauty that is never old ; The gift to sing ; To America / Damien Sneed -- April song ; Lost illusions ; Southern mansion / Jeremiah Evans -- I know my soul ; Dance of love / Brandon Spencer -- Songs of the seasons / Margaret Bonds -- Supplication ; Compensation ; My people / Joel Thompson -- Peace ; Invocation / Jasmine Barnes -- Romance / Shawn Ehireime Okpebholo -- Desire song cycle ; Silver rain cycle / Robert Owens.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">For this album, "Brownlee has commissioned six of today's leading African-American composers - Damien Sneed, Brandon Spencer, Jasmine Barnes, Joel Thompson, and Shawn E. Okpebholo - to set poetry from the Harlem Renaissance to song, including poems by... Claude McKay, Langston Hughes, James Weldon Johnson, and more. The songs revolve around themes of joy, empowerment, faith, love, and strength in the face of challenge. "--Singer's website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
